{"name":"Trixter","hex":"#705676","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[],"entries":[{"title":"Trixter","blocks":[{"text":"Trixter is an American hard rock band formed in 1983 in Paramus, New Jersey. The band gained popularity in the early 1990s with hits like \"Give It to Me Good\" that peaked at number 65 on the Billboard Hot 100 in 1990 and \"One in a Million\". Despite lineup changes and a hiatus in the late 90s, Trixter has maintained a presence in the rock scene through tours and occasional album releases."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f9/Trixter_2015.png/330px-Trixter_2015.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Trixter"},{"title":"Trixter (album)","blocks":[{"text":"Trixter is the debut album of the band Trixter. It attained gold status, reaching No. 28 on the Billboard 200 chart. The album spawned three minor hit singles on the Billboard Hot 100: \"Give It to Me Good\" at No. 65, \"Surrender\" at No. 72, and \"One in a Million\" at No. 75."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/f/f1/Trixter_self_titled.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Trixter_(album)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d2/Steve_Brown.png/330px-Steve_Brown.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d2/Steve_Brown.png/330px-Steve_Brown.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASteve_Brown.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4a/PJ_Farley.png/500px-PJ_Farley.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4a/PJ_Farley.png/1280px-PJ_Farley.png?u